    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6788" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακουφ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lift</i> or <i>raise up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δέμας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					218
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑαυτὸν εἰς ἀνάβασιν,</span> of
			a horseman mounting, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				7.2
			</span></i>; of the ship of state, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κάρα βυθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀὴρ ἀ. τὸν ἀσκόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					939a35
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>feel lightened</i> or <i>lifted up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεκουφίσθην δέμας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1392
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be relieved in mind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.2.28
			</span></i>.</div>
